    "status": "completed",
    "turns": 36,
    "tool_calls": 36,
    "summary": "Fixed the wfmt package with the following changes:\n\n1. **varint.py**: Fixed `decode_uvarint` to properly handle multi-byte LEB128 encoding (was only reading single byte with 0x7F mask). Now correctly accumulates 7-bit groups with continuation bit handling.\n\n2. **header.py**: Changed count field encoding from big-endian (`>I`) to little-endian (`<I`) to match the sample files.\n\n3. **crc.py**: Added final XOR with 0xFFFFFFFF to `compute_crc` to produce standard CRC-32 (was missing, producing non-standard variant). Also changed `unpack_crc` to raise `WFormatError` instead of `ValueError`.\n\n4. **codec.py**: Added CRC verification in `unpack()` - now checks stored CRC against computed CRC before parsing records. Raises `WFormatError(kind=\"checksum\")` on mismatch. All error paths use `WFormatError` with appropriate `kind` values.\n\n5. **stream.py**: Completely rewrote `iter_records` to be truly streaming/lazy - reads fixed-size chunks via `read(n)` instead of loading entire file with `read()`",
    "changed_workspace": true
  },
